{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '345,405p' ../agent-source/internal/transport/transport.go; sed -n '1,85p' /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/core/events.py\"","aggregated_output":"// Send asynchronously sends raft messages to their target nodes.\n//\n// The generic async send Go pattern used in Send() is found in CockroachDB's\n// codebase.\nfunc (t *Transport) Send(req pb.Message) bool {\n\tv, _ := t.send(req)\n\tif !v {\n\t\tt.metrics.messageSendFailure(1)\n\t}\n\treturn v\n}\n\nfunc (t *Transport) send(req pb.Message) (bool, failedSend) {\n\tif req.Type == pb.InstallSnapshot {\n\t\tpanic(\"snapshot message must be sent via its own channel.\")\n\t}\n\ttoNodeID := req.To\n\tclusterID := req.ClusterId\n\tfrom := req.From\n\taddr, key, err := t.resolver.Resolve(clusterID, toNodeID)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tplog.Warningf(\"%s do not have the address for %s, dropping a message\",\n\t\t\tt.sourceID, dn(clusterID, toNodeID))\n\t\treturn false, unknownTarget\n\t}\n\t// fail fast\n\tif !t.GetCircuitBreaker(addr).Ready() {\n\t\tt.metrics.messageConnectionFailure()\n\t\treturn false, circuitBreakerNotReady\n\t}\n\t// get the channel, create it in case it is not in the queue map\n\tt.mu.Lock()\n\tsq, ok := t.mu.queues[key]\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tsq = sendQueue{\n\t\t\tch: make(chan pb.Message, sendQueueLen),\n\t\t\trl: server.NewRateLimiter(t.nhConfig.MaxSendQueueSize),\n\t\t}\n\t\tt.mu.queues[key] = sq\n\t}\n\tt.mu.Unlock()\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tshutdownQueue := func() {\n\t\t\tt.mu.Lock()\n\t\t\tdelete(t.mu.queues, key)\n\t\t\tt.mu.Unlock()\n\t\t}\n\t\tt.stopper.RunWorker(func() {\n\t\t\taffected := make(nodeMap)\n\t\t\tif !t.connectAndProcess(addr, sq, from, affected) {\n\t\t\t\tt.notifyUnreachable(addr, affected)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tshutdownQueue()\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\tif sq.rateLimited() {\n\t\treturn false, rateLimited\n\t}\n\n\tsq.increase(req)\n\n\"\"\"Bounded event lookup and correlation, independent of workflow and tools.\"\"\"\nfrom .proposals import EventRequirement, Comparison\n\nMISSING = object()\n\n\ndef field(event, path):\n    '''Retrieve a nested field from an event dictionary using dot-separated path.'''\n    value = event\n    for key in path.split('.'):\n        if not isinstance(value,dict) or key not in value:\n            return MISSING\n        value = value[key]\n    return value\n\n\ndef compare(event, condition, aliases=None):\n    '''Compare a field in an event against a condition, optionally using aliases for other events.'''\n    left = field(event,condition.field)\n    right = condition.value\n    if condition.reference:\n        alias, sep, path = condition.reference.partition('.')\n        if not sep or alias not in (aliases or {}): return None\n        right = field(aliases[alias],path) # type: ignore\n    if left is MISSING or right is MISSING: return None\n    equal = type(left) is type(right) and left == right\n    return equal if condition.op == 'eq' else not equal\n\n\ndef event_requirements(requirements, reference=None):\n    '''Order and validate a list of event requirements, ensuring unique aliases and no causal cycles.'''\n    requirements = [EventRequirement.model_validate(r) for r in requirements]\n    aliases = {r.alias for r in requirements}\n    if len(aliases) != len(requirements) or any(not a or '.' in a for a in aliases):\n        raise ValueError('Prerequisite aliases must be unique nonempty names')\n    references = [c.reference for r in requirements for c in r.conditions if c.reference]\n    if reference: references.append(reference)\n    if any(ref.partition('.')[0] not in aliases or not ref.partition('.')[2] for ref in references):\n        raise ValueError('Comparison references an unavailable prerequisite alias or field')\n    ordered, pending = [], list(requirements)\n    while pending:\n        ready = next((r for r in pending if all(not c.reference or c.reference.partition('.')[0] in {a.alias for a in ordered} for c in r.conditions)),None)\n        if ready is None: raise ValueError('Prerequisite references contain a causal cycle')\n        ordered.append(ready); pending.remove(ready)\n    return ordered\n\n\ndef match_prerequisites(events, requirements, witness_index=None, identity_fields=()):\n    '''Match a sequence of events against a set of ordered prerequisites, optionally using a witness event for identity checks.'''\n    if not requirements:\n        return {'status':'unknown','reason':'No correlated prerequisite specification','matched_indices':[], 'alias_indices':{}}\n    try: ordered = event_requirements(requirements)\n    except ValueError as exc:\n        return {'status':'unknown','reason':str(exc),'matched_indices':[], 'alias_indices':{}}\n    missing, matches, absent = False, [], set()\n    witness = events[witness_index] if witness_index is not None else None\n    witness_stream = witness.get('_ca_stream') if witness is not None else None\n    def search(step, indices):\n        nonlocal missing\n        if step == len(ordered):\n            matches.append(indices); return\n        req = ordered[step]\n        aliases = {alias:events[index] for alias,index in indices.items()}\n        predecessors = [indices[c.reference.partition('.')[0]] for c in req.conditions if c.reference]\n        selected_streams = {events[index].get('_ca_stream') for index in indices.values()}\n        for index,event in enumerate(events[:witness_index] if witness_index is not None else events):\n            if event.get('event') != req.event or index in indices.values(): continue\n            stream = event.get('_ca_stream')\n            if witness is not None and stream != witness_stream: continue\n            if selected_streams and stream not in selected_streams: continue\n            if any(index <= prior for prior in predecessors): continue\n            identity = [compare(event,Comparison(field=k,reference='witness.'+k),{'witness':witness}) for k in identity_fields] if witness is not None else []\n            if any(v is False for v in identity): continue\n            checks = identity + [compare(event,c,aliases) for c in req.conditions]\n            if any(v is False for v in checks): continue\n            if any(v is None for v in checks):\n                missing = True\n                absent.update(req.alias+'.'+k for k,v in zip(identity_fields,identity) if v is None)\n                absent.update(req.alias+'.'+c.field+(' / '+c.reference if c.reference else '')\n                    for c in req.conditions if compare(event,c,aliases) is None)\n                continue\n            search(step+1,{**indices,req.alias:index})\n            if len(matches) >= (2 if witness is not None else 1): return\n    search(0,{})\n    ambiguous = witness is not None and (len(matches)>1 or missing)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_read_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));c=r['candidates'][0];q=c['question'].copy();q['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['unknowns']=[]\nclaim='O-read-response-context';binding='K-read-response-context'\nsource_ids=['S-readqueue','S-readreply','S-readforward','S-readconsumer','S-readcaller','S-readtest','S-readcontract','S-followerreadtest']\nground=dict(source_ids=['S-readqueue','S-readreply','S-readforward','S-readconsumer','S-readcaller'],expectation_ids=['S-readtest','S-followerreadtest','S-readcontract'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='The tracker returns each qualified readStatus with its own context and origin (S-readtest explicitly expects distinct contexts for a released prefix). The follower exports exactly the reply context, and the client consumer matches only that context. Therefore a reply reporting qualification to a requesting replica must preserve that request context. Index promotion to a later safe index is allowed; substituting identity is not equivalent to that promotion.',applicability='Multi-voter leader, current-term commitment, stable term/membership, distinct contexts admitted from remote members and actually removed by one quorum confirmation. This is a local response-correlation duty, not a promise that all network requests succeed before a deadline.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Local completion already uses each record context; the single-voter branch is outside this queued-prefix check.','Packet loss or client timeout alone would not violate this requirement.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='When a current multi-voter leader releases a pending remote ReadIndex request after quorum confirmation and emits its ReadIndexResp to the requesting replica, the response must carry that released request\\\\u2019s SystemCtx unchanged, including when one confirmation releases several queued requests. The returned index may be advanced to the later confirmed safe index.',source_ids=source_ids,scope=dict(description='Local correlation of an actually released remote read request to its emitted ReadIndexResp in a stable leader term and membership.',assumptions=['Crash-fault operation with unmodified messages produced by configured peers.','Distinct nonzero SystemCtx values identify the pending requests; source identity and term are preserved through delivery.'],excluded=['Numeric completion deadlines or unconditional read availability','End-to-end client timeout measurement','Wrong read values or linearizability violations','Restart and concurrent membership change during the confirmation']),pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbind=dict(id=binding,material_id='S-readreply',symbol='raft.handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',start_line=1771,end_line=1790,description='Consumes confirmed readStatus records and emits per-origin ReadIndexResp or local ReadyToRead.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=source_ids,rationale='The per-origin response builder is the concrete consumer of each qualified request and its correlation identity.')])\nnewsrc=[]\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):newsrc.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k))\nfor x in [('S-testlogdb','internal/raft/logdb_test.go',24,60),('S-testlogentries','internal/raft/logdb_test.go',91,156),('S-bootstrap','internal/raft/peer.go',360,407),('S-peerapply','internal/raft/peer.go',136,165),('S-updatecommit','internal/raft/peer.go',409,431),('S-peerread','internal/raft/peer.go',298,312),('S-ticks','internal/raft/raft.go',559,630),('S-transportloss','internal/transport/transport.go',345,403)]:src(*x)\nlegality=dict(source_ids=['S-peerlaunch','S-bootstrap','S-peerapply','S-update','S-updatecommit','S-peerread','S-testlogdb','S-testlogentries','S-ticks','S-peer','S-engine','S-send','S-transportloss','S-readqueue','S-readreply'],expectation_ids=['S-dbcontract','S-readtest'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='Launch three initial/new peers with identical unique bootstrap addresses and empty TestLogDBs. The synchronous driver saves entries/state before transmitting any update messages, applies only committed bootstrap AddNode configurations, commits updates, and notifies lastApplied. Tick only replica 1 until real vote exchange elects it and current-term no-op is committed/applied at all peers. No private Raft field or handler is substituted; private state is sampled only for prerequisite diagnostics. The driver issues Peer.ReadIndex on followers 2 and 3 with distinct nonzero contexts. A fixed policy discards context-101 heartbeats before delivery; retained messages share one FIFO. The first dropped heartbeat batch leaves its request pending, and the next context heartbeat is delivered and answered by real follower handlers. Loss is permitted by the asynchronous transport send boundary; no fabricated reply, stale authority or reorder is needed. TestLogDB implements the acquired ILogDB boundary; there is no crash in this history. Holding replication until after save is a permissible stronger persistence order, and it occurs in the setup rather than serializing the investigated read overlap.',applicability='One single-threaded test owns all Peer calls, storage, queue and observation fields. No goroutines, background timers, external clients or shutdown-dependent observations. Both requests have distinct origins, one outstanding request per origin, making To an independent unambiguous response identity. Generated contexts are valid values allowed by Peer.ReadIndex and node context generation; test bypasses random selection only.',unresolved=['This driver does not execute NodeHost client batching or timeout callbacks; their exact-context consumer behavior is source-grounded only.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Earlier source-only reading excluded a cumulative client-context consumer mechanism. A Node